@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ito-il30-nouns`
IMPORT `ito-88-definitions`
IMPORT `ito-top-layer`
IMPORT `ito-91-capital-gains`
IMPORT `retl-48a-betterment-tax`

-- Tests for the Real Estate Taxation Law ss 6 and 48A (the betterment tax). Every expected value was worked by hand from the Law's text and definitions
-- (the arithmetic is beside each group) before it was run. A failing assertion is a finding. All amounts are HYPOTHETICAL.

§ `Tests of section 48A`

§§ `Fixtures`

GIVEN u IS A NUMBER
      r IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `A band of a marginal scale`
`a band ending at` u `at the rate` r MEANS
    `A band of a marginal scale` WITH
        `upper limit of the band` IS JUST u
        `rate of the band`        IS r

GIVEN r IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `A band of a marginal scale`
`a last band at the rate` r MEANS
    `A band of a marginal scale` WITH
        `upper limit of the band` IS NOTHING
        `rate of the band`        IS r

`the scale of s 121(a)` MEANS
    LIST `a band ending at` 301_200 `at the rate` (31%),
         `a band ending at` 560_280 `at the rate` (35%),
         `a last band at the rate` (47%)

`the scale of s 121(b)(1)` MEANS
    LIST `a band ending at` 84_120 `at the rate` (10%),
         `a band ending at` 120_720 `at the rate` (14%),
         `a band ending at` 228_000 `at the rate` (20%),
         `a band ending at` 301_200 `at the rate` (31%),
         `a band ending at` 560_280 `at the rate` (35%),
         `a last band at the rate` (47%)

`a flat scale at 47%` MEANS LIST `a last band at the rate` (47%)

GIVEN f IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Holdings of means of control in one body of persons`
`a profits holding of` f MEANS
    `Holdings of means of control in one body of persons` WITH
        `fraction of the right to profits`                                              IS f
        `fraction of the right to appoint a director or general manager`                IS 0
        `fraction of the voting rights in the general meeting`                          IS 0
        `fraction of the right to a share of the surplus assets on winding up`          IS 0
        `fraction of the right to direct the holder of a right in (1) to (4) on how to use it` IS 0

GIVETH A LIST OF `A person who may hold together with the person`
`no others` MEANS EMPTY

GIVEN d IS A DATE
      f IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `The holdings of a person on one day`
`a profits record on` d `of` f MEANS
    `The holdings of a person on one day` WITH
        `the day` IS d
        `the person's own holdings that day` IS `a profits holding of` f
        `the others who may hold together with the person that day` IS `no others`

GIVETH A LIST OF `The holdings of a person on one day`
`no records` MEANS EMPTY

-- The readings: every fork named, or declined.
GIVEN c  IS A `A reading of how the days of a period are counted`
      t  IS A `A reading of a cap on the rate where the gain stands in several bands`
      v1 IS A `A reading of the years counted from 1949 in section 91(f)(1)`
      v2 IS A `A reading of the years counted from 2005 in section 91(f)(2)`
      l1 IS A `A reading of how a tax year of the Real Estate Taxation Law is named`
GIVETH A `The readings of the forks in sections 88, 91, 125B and 125C`
`the readings: days` c `, cap` t `, years from 1949` v1 `, years from 2005` v2 `, naming` l1 MEANS
    `The readings of the forks in sections 88, 91, 125B and 125C` WITH
        `together with another`                   IS `declined where the number of others changes the answer`
        `counting the days of a period`           IS c
        `half the holding expenses`               IS `declined where half the holding expenses changes the answer`
        `the twelve months before a day`          IS `declined where the first day of the twelve months changes the answer`
        `the years from 1949 in section 91(f)(1)` IS v1
        `the years from 2005 in section 91(f)(2)` IS v2
        `a cap where the gain stands in several bands` IS t
        `where each part stands in the top layer` IS `declined where the order of the parts changes the answer`
        `the time of the test in section 125B(3)` IS `declined where the time of the test changes the answer`
        `the time of the test in section 91(b)(3)` IS `declined where the time of the sale test changes the answer`
        `the real gain for the middle part`       IS `declined where the real gain used for the middle part changes the answer`
        `the naming of a tax year of the Real Estate Taxation Law` IS l1

`the default readings` MEANS
    `the readings: days` `declined where the way of counting changes the answer` `, cap` `declined where the way of applying the cap changes the answer` `, years from 1949` `declined where the number of years changes the answer` `, years from 2005` `declined where the number of years changes the answer` `, naming` `declined where the naming of the tax year changes the answer`

GIVEN c IS A `A reading of how the days of a period are counted`
GIVETH A `The readings of the forks in sections 88, 91, 125B and 125C`
`the default readings but the days counted as` c MEANS
    `the readings: days` c `, cap` `declined where the way of applying the cap changes the answer` `, years from 1949` `declined where the number of years changes the answer` `, years from 2005` `declined where the number of years changes the answer` `, naming` `declined where the naming of the tax year changes the answer`

GIVEN l1 IS A `A reading of how a tax year of the Real Estate Taxation Law is named`
      v2 IS A `A reading of the years counted from 2005 in section 91(f)(2)`
GIVETH A `The readings of the forks in sections 88, 91, 125B and 125C`
`the default readings but the tax years named as` l1 `and counted from 2005 as` v2 MEANS
    `the readings: days` `declined where the way of counting changes the answer` `, cap` `declined where the way of applying the cap changes the answer` `, years from 1949` `declined where the number of years changes the answer` `, years from 2005` v2 `, naming` l1

GIVEN t IS A `A reading of a cap on the rate where the gain stands in several bands`
GIVETH A `The readings of the forks in sections 88, 91, 125B and 125C`
`the default readings but the cap read as` t MEANS
    `the readings: days` `declined where the way of counting changes the answer` `, cap` t `, years from 1949` `declined where the number of years changes the answer` `, years from 2005` `declined where the number of years changes the answer` `, naming` `declined where the naming of the tax year changes the answer`

-- A sale, with every field.
GIVEN seller IS A `The seller, for section 91`
      assoc  IS A BOOLEAN
      bett   IS A NUMBER
      rbett  IS A NUMBER
      cinfl  IS A NUMBER
      bought IS A DATE
      sold   IS A DATE
      qual   IS A BOOLEAN
      b4     IS A BOOLEAN
      b3     IS A BOOLEAN
      dirrate IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      excl   IS A BOOLEAN
      company IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `A sale of a right in land, for section 48A`
`the land sale by` seller `, land association action` assoc `, betterment` bett `, real betterment` rbett `, chargeable inflationary` cinfl `, bought` bought `, sold` sold `, qualifying apartment` qual `, (b4) conditions` b4 `, (b3) building rights` b3 `, the Director allowed` dirrate `, (d)(4) excludes` excl `, company or liquidation` company MEANS
    `A sale of a right in land, for section 48A` WITH
        `the seller` IS seller
        `it is an action in a land association` IS assoc
        `the betterment` IS bett
        `the real betterment` IS rbett
        `the chargeable inflationary amount` IS cinfl
        `the purchase day` IS bought
        `the sale day` IS sold
        `it is a qualifying residential apartment that section 48A(b2) governs` IS qual
        `the conditions of section 48A(b4) hold` IS b4
        `the consideration was influenced by additional building rights, section 48A(b3)` IS b3
        `the Director allowed in writing a rate lower than the cap, of` IS dirrate
        `section 48A(d)(4) excludes the sale` IS excl
        `the seller is a company with business income, or an individual who received the right when a company was wound up` IS company

-- A plain sale: no association, no apartment, nothing excluded.
GIVEN seller IS A `The seller, for section 91`
      rbett  IS A NUMBER
      cinfl  IS A NUMBER
      bought IS A DATE
      sold   IS A DATE
GIVETH A `A sale of a right in land, for section 48A`
`a plain land sale by` seller `, real betterment` rbett `, chargeable inflationary` cinfl `, bought` bought `, sold` sold MEANS
    `the land sale by` seller `, land association action` FALSE `, betterment` (rbett TIMES 2) `, real betterment` rbett `, chargeable inflationary` cinfl `, bought` bought `, sold` sold `, qualifying apartment` FALSE `, (b4) conditions` FALSE `, (b3) building rights` FALSE `, the Director allowed` NOTHING `, (d)(4) excludes` FALSE `, company or liquidation` FALSE

GIVEN recs IS A LIST OF `The holdings of a person on one day`
GIVETH A `The seller, for section 91`
`an individual with the records` recs MEANS `an individual` recs

GIVEN rate IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `The seller, for section 91`
`a body of persons taxed at` rate MEANS `a body of persons` rate

`someone with no records` MEANS `an individual with the records` `no records`

`the sale day of the tests` MEANS YMD 2026 6 30

§§ `Section 6(b): the betterment`
-- Sale value 1,000,000 over a remaining purchase value of 700,000: 300,000.  Not above it: nought.
#ASSERT `s 6(b) — the betterment on a sale value of` 1_000_000 `over a remaining purchase value of` 700_000 EQUALS 300_000
#ASSERT `s 6(b) — the betterment on a sale value of` 700_000 `over a remaining purchase value of` 700_000 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `s 6(b) — the betterment on a sale value of` 500_000 `over a remaining purchase value of` 700_000 EQUALS 0

§§ `Paragraph (b)(1), (1A), (2): the cap`
-- Bought 1 May 2013, sold 30 June 2026 (not (b1)). Other income 0, scale (a): the real betterment 200,000 in the 31% band, capped at 25%: 50,000.
#ASSERT `retl 48A — the betterment tax on` (`a plain land sale by` `someone with no records` `, real betterment` 200_000 `, chargeable inflationary` 0 `, bought` (YMD 2013 5 1) `, sold` `the sale day of the tests`) `, the highest rate of section 121 being` (47%) `, the seller's other taxable income being` 0 `under the scale` `the scale of s 121(a)` `, reading the forks as` `the default readings` EQUALS 50_000
-- With a chargeable inflationary amount of 20,000: + 10% = 2,000.
#ASSERT `retl 48A — the betterment tax on` (`a plain land sale by` `someone with no records` `, real betterment` 200_000 `, chargeable inflationary` 20_000 `, bought` (YMD 2013 5 1) `, sold` `the sale day of the tests`) `, the highest rate of section 121 being` (47%) `, the seller's other taxable income being` 0 `under the scale` `the scale of s 121(a)` `, reading the forks as` `the default readings` EQUALS 52_000
-- An action in a land association by a material shareholder (10% on the sale day): 30% of 200,000 = 60,000 ; not a material shareholder: 25% = 50,000 ;
-- a material shareholder but not an action in a land association: 25%.
#ASSERT `retl 48A — the betterment tax on` (`the land sale by` (`an individual with the records` (LIST `a profits record on` `the sale day of the tests` `of` (10%))) `, land association action` TRUE `, betterment` 300_000 `, real betterment` 200_000 `, chargeable inflationary` 0 `, bought` (YMD 2013 5 1) `, sold` `the sale day of the tests` `, qualifying apartment` FALSE `, (b4) conditions` FALSE `, (b3) building rights` FALSE `, the Director allowed` NOTHING `, (d)(4) excludes` FALSE `, company or liquidation` FALSE) `, the highest rate of section 121 being` (47%) `, the seller's other taxable income being` 0 `under the scale` `the scale of s 121(a)` `, reading the forks as` `the default readings` EQUALS 60_000
#ASSERT `retl 48A — the betterment tax on` (`the land sale by` (`an individual with the records` `no records`) `, land association action` TRUE `, betterment` 300_000 `, real betterment` 200_000 `, chargeable inflationary` 0 `, bought` (YMD 2013 5 1) `, sold` `the sale day of the tests` `, qualifying apartment` FALSE `, (b4) conditions` FALSE `, (b3) building rights` FALSE `, the Director allowed` NOTHING `, (d)(4) excludes` FALSE `, company or liquidation` FALSE) `, the highest rate of section 121 being` (47%) `, the seller's other taxable income being` 0 `under the scale` `the scale of s 121(a)` `, reading the forks as` `the default readings` EQUALS 50_000
#ASSERT `retl 48A — the betterment tax on` (`the land sale by` (`an individual with the records` (LIST `a profits record on` `the sale day of the tests` `of` (10%))) `, land association action` FALSE `, betterment` 300_000 `, real betterment` 200_000 `, chargeable inflationary` 0 `, bought` (YMD 2013 5 1) `, sold` `the sale day of the tests` `, qualifying apartment` FALSE `, (b4) conditions` FALSE `, (b3) building rights` FALSE `, the Director allowed` NOTHING `, (d)(4) excludes` FALSE `, company or liquidation` FALSE) `, the highest rate of section 121 being` (47%) `, the seller's other taxable income being` 0 `under the scale` `the scale of s 121(a)` `, reading the forks as` `the default readings` EQUALS 50_000
-- The twelve months (fork S4): a record on 30 June 2025 is inside one reading only: 60,000 or 50,000: refused.
#ASSERT REFUSED `retl 48A — the betterment tax on` (`the land sale by` (`an individual with the records` (LIST `a profits record on` (YMD 2025 6 30) `of` (10%))) `, land association action` TRUE `, betterment` 300_000 `, real betterment` 200_000 `, chargeable inflationary` 0 `, bought` (YMD 2013 5 1) `, sold` `the sale day of the tests` `, qualifying apartment` FALSE `, (b4) conditions` FALSE `, (b3) building rights` FALSE `, the Director allowed` NOTHING `, (d)(4) excludes` FALSE `, company or liquidation` FALSE) `, the highest rate of section 121 being` (47%) `, the seller's other taxable income being` 0 `under the scale` `the scale of s 121(a)` `, reading the forks as` `the default readings` BECAUSE "section 48A or section 88 leaves open a reading (the layer, the cap, the days of a period, who is a material shareholder, the naming of a tax year, or the years of paragraph (d)), and here the tax turns on it"
-- (b)(2): the Director allowed 20% (lower than 25%): 20% x 200,000 = 40,000 ; allowed 30% (not lower): the cap 25% stands: 50,000.
#ASSERT `retl 48A — the betterment tax on` (`the land sale by` (`an individual with the records` `no records`) `, land association action` FALSE `, betterment` 300_000 `, real betterment` 200_000 `, chargeable inflationary` 0 `, bought` (YMD 2013 5 1) `, sold` `the sale day of the tests` `, qualifying apartment` FALSE `, (b4) conditions` FALSE `, (b3) building rights` FALSE `, the Director allowed` (JUST (20%)) `, (d)(4) excludes` FALSE `, company or liquidation` FALSE) `, the highest rate of section 121 being` (47%) `, the seller's other taxable income being` 0 `under the scale` `the scale of s 121(a)` `, reading the forks as` `the default readings` EQUALS 40_000
#ASSERT `retl 48A — the betterment tax on` (`the land sale by` (`an individual with the records` `no records`) `, land association action` FALSE `, betterment` 300_000 `, real betterment` 200_000 `, chargeable inflationary` 0 `, bought` (YMD 2013 5 1) `, sold` `the sale day of the tests` `, qualifying apartment` FALSE `, (b4) conditions` FALSE `, (b3) building rights` FALSE `, the Director allowed` (JUST (30%)) `, (d)(4) excludes` FALSE `, company or liquidation` FALSE) `, the highest rate of section 121 being` (47%) `, the seller's other taxable income being` 0 `under the scale` `the scale of s 121(a)` `, reading the forks as` `the default readings` EQUALS 50_000
-- Fork T1: other income 220,000, real betterment 100,000, scale (b)(1): 24,600 (each band capped) or 25,000 (the average): refused by default.
#ASSERT REFUSED `retl 48A — the betterment tax on` (`a plain land sale by` `someone with no records` `, real betterment` 100_000 `, chargeable inflationary` 0 `, bought` (YMD 2013 5 1) `, sold` `the sale day of the tests`) `, the highest rate of section 121 being` (47%) `, the seller's other taxable income being` 220_000 `under the scale` `the scale of s 121(b)(1)` `, reading the forks as` `the default readings` BECAUSE "section 48A or section 88 leaves open a reading (the layer, the cap, the days of a period, who is a material shareholder, the naming of a tax year, or the years of paragraph (d)), and here the tax turns on it"
#ASSERT `retl 48A — the betterment tax on` (`a plain land sale by` `someone with no records` `, real betterment` 100_000 `, chargeable inflationary` 0 `, bought` (YMD 2013 5 1) `, sold` `the sale day of the tests`) `, the highest rate of section 121 being` (47%) `, the seller's other taxable income being` 220_000 `under the scale` `the scale of s 121(b)(1)` `, reading the forks as` (`the default readings but the cap read as` `the rate of each band is capped`) EQUALS 24_600

§§ `Paragraph (a): a body of persons`
-- 23% (an input) x 200,000 = 46,000 ; with a chargeable inflationary amount of 20,000: + 2,000 = 48,000.
#ASSERT `retl 48A — the betterment tax on` (`a plain land sale by` (`a body of persons taxed at` (23%)) `, real betterment` 200_000 `, chargeable inflationary` 0 `, bought` (YMD 2013 5 1) `, sold` `the sale day of the tests`) `, the highest rate of section 121 being` (47%) `, the seller's other taxable income being` 0 `under the scale` `the scale of s 121(a)` `, reading the forks as` `the default readings` EQUALS 46_000
#ASSERT `retl 48A — the betterment tax on` (`a plain land sale by` (`a body of persons taxed at` (23%)) `, real betterment` 200_000 `, chargeable inflationary` 20_000 `, bought` (YMD 2013 5 1) `, sold` `the sale day of the tests`) `, the highest rate of section 121 being` (47%) `, the seller's other taxable income being` 0 `under the scale` `the scale of s 121(a)` `, reading the forks as` `the default readings` EQUALS 48_000

§§ `Paragraph (b1): the three parts (flat scale at 47%, the highest rate of section 121 being 47%)`
-- Bought 11 February 1999, sold 17 July 2015 (6,000 days later); the commencement day 7 November 2001 is 1,000 days after the purchase.
--   The real betterment 36,006,000 = 6,000 x 6,001. From the commencement day to the day before the change date (31 December 2011): 3,706 days (3,707 counting both ends).
--   Days between:  part 1 = 36,006,000 x 1,000/6,000 = 6,001,000 ; part 2 = x 3,706/6,000 = 22,239,706 ; part 3 = the rest = 7,765,294.
--                  tax = 47% x 6,001,000 (2,820,470) + 20% x 22,239,706 (4,447,941.2) + 25% x 7,765,294 (1,941,323.5) = 9,209,734.7.
--   Both ends counted, the Starting Day in the part after it (0.1.1: the parts must partition the days, so no day is in two): part 1 = x 1,000/6,001 = 6,000,000 ; part 2 = x 3,707/6,001 = 22,242,000 ; part 3 = 7,764,000.
--                  tax = 47% x 6,000,000 (2,820,000) + 20% x 22,242,000 (4,448,400) + 25% x 7,764,000 (1,941,000) = 9,209,400.
--   Both ends counted, the Starting Day in the part before it: part 1 = x 1,001/6,001 = 6,006,000 ; part 2 = x 3,706/6,001 = 22,236,000 ; part 3 = 7,764,000 ;
--                  tax = 47% x 6,006,000 (2,822,820) + 20% x 22,236,000 (4,447,200) + 25% x 7,764,000 (1,941,000) = 9,211,020.
#ASSERT `retl 48A — the betterment tax on` (`a plain land sale by` `someone with no records` `, real betterment` 36_006_000 `, chargeable inflationary` 0 `, bought` (YMD 1999 2 11) `, sold` (YMD 2015 7 17)) `, the highest rate of section 121 being` (47%) `, the seller's other taxable income being` 0 `under the scale` `a flat scale at 47%` `, reading the forks as` (`the default readings but the days counted as` `the days between the first day and the last day, the first not counted`) EQUALS 9_209_734.7
#ASSERT `retl 48A — the betterment tax on` (`a plain land sale by` `someone with no records` `, real betterment` 36_006_000 `, chargeable inflationary` 0 `, bought` (YMD 1999 2 11) `, sold` (YMD 2015 7 17)) `, the highest rate of section 121 being` (47%) `, the seller's other taxable income being` 0 `under the scale` `a flat scale at 47%` `, reading the forks as` (`the default readings but the days counted as` `both the first and the last day are counted`) EQUALS 9_209_400
#ASSERT `retl 48A — the betterment tax on` (`a plain land sale by` `someone with no records` `, real betterment` 36_006_000 `, chargeable inflationary` 0 `, bought` (YMD 1999 2 11) `, sold` (YMD 2015 7 17)) `, the highest rate of section 121 being` (47%) `, the seller's other taxable income being` 0 `under the scale` `a flat scale at 47%` `, reading the forks as` (`the default readings but the days counted as` `both ends counted, a boundary day belonging to the part before it`) EQUALS 9_211_020
#ASSERT REFUSED `retl 48A — the betterment tax on` (`a plain land sale by` `someone with no records` `, real betterment` 36_006_000 `, chargeable inflationary` 0 `, bought` (YMD 1999 2 11) `, sold` (YMD 2015 7 17)) `, the highest rate of section 121 being` (47%) `, the seller's other taxable income being` 0 `under the scale` `a flat scale at 47%` `, reading the forks as` `the default readings` BECAUSE "section 48A or section 88 leaves open a reading (the layer, the cap, the days of a period, who is a material shareholder, the naming of a tax year, or the years of paragraph (d)), and here the tax turns on it"

§§ `Paragraph (b2): a qualifying apartment bought before the transition day`
-- Bought 1 January 2010, sold 1 January 2020 (3,652 days; the transition day 1 January 2014 is 1,461 days after the purchase). Real betterment 13,340,756 = 3,652 x 3,653.
--   Days between: exempt 13,340,756 x 1,461/3,652 = 5,337,033 ; the rest 8,003,723 at 25% (flat scale) = 2,000,930.75. A chargeable inflationary amount: 0%.
--   Both ends, the Transition Day in the rest (0.1.1): exempt x 1,461/3,653 = 3,652 x 1,461 = 5,335,572 ; the rest 8,005,184 at 25% = 2,001,296.
--   Both ends, the Transition Day in the exempt part: exempt x 1,462/3,653 = 5,339,224 ; the rest 8,001,532 at 25% = 2,000,383.
#ASSERT `retl 48A — the betterment tax on` (`the land sale by` (`an individual with the records` `no records`) `, land association action` FALSE `, betterment` 20_000_000 `, real betterment` 13_340_756 `, chargeable inflationary` 500_000 `, bought` (YMD 2010 1 1) `, sold` (YMD 2020 1 1) `, qualifying apartment` TRUE `, (b4) conditions` FALSE `, (b3) building rights` FALSE `, the Director allowed` NOTHING `, (d)(4) excludes` FALSE `, company or liquidation` FALSE) `, the highest rate of section 121 being` (47%) `, the seller's other taxable income being` 0 `under the scale` `a flat scale at 47%` `, reading the forks as` (`the default readings but the days counted as` `the days between the first day and the last day, the first not counted`) EQUALS 2_000_930.75
#ASSERT `retl 48A — the betterment tax on` (`the land sale by` (`an individual with the records` `no records`) `, land association action` FALSE `, betterment` 20_000_000 `, real betterment` 13_340_756 `, chargeable inflationary` 500_000 `, bought` (YMD 2010 1 1) `, sold` (YMD 2020 1 1) `, qualifying apartment` TRUE `, (b4) conditions` FALSE `, (b3) building rights` FALSE `, the Director allowed` NOTHING `, (d)(4) excludes` FALSE `, company or liquidation` FALSE) `, the highest rate of section 121 being` (47%) `, the seller's other taxable income being` 0 `under the scale` `a flat scale at 47%` `, reading the forks as` (`the default readings but the days counted as` `both the first and the last day are counted`) EQUALS 2_001_296
#ASSERT `retl 48A — the betterment tax on` (`the land sale by` (`an individual with the records` `no records`) `, land association action` FALSE `, betterment` 20_000_000 `, real betterment` 13_340_756 `, chargeable inflationary` 500_000 `, bought` (YMD 2010 1 1) `, sold` (YMD 2020 1 1) `, qualifying apartment` TRUE `, (b4) conditions` FALSE `, (b3) building rights` FALSE `, the Director allowed` NOTHING `, (d)(4) excludes` FALSE `, company or liquidation` FALSE) `, the highest rate of section 121 being` (47%) `, the seller's other taxable income being` 0 `under the scale` `a flat scale at 47%` `, reading the forks as` (`the default readings but the days counted as` `both ends counted, a boundary day belonging to the part before it`) EQUALS 2_000_383
-- (b4): the conditions hold: (b)(1) applies, not (b2) or (b3). Bought 1 January 2013 (after the change date, so (b1) is not in play), sold 1 January 2020:
-- 13,340,756 x 25% = 3,335,189 ; the chargeable inflationary amount 500,000 x 10% = 50,000: 3,385,189.
#ASSERT `retl 48A — the betterment tax on` (`the land sale by` (`an individual with the records` `no records`) `, land association action` FALSE `, betterment` 20_000_000 `, real betterment` 13_340_756 `, chargeable inflationary` 500_000 `, bought` (YMD 2013 1 1) `, sold` (YMD 2020 1 1) `, qualifying apartment` TRUE `, (b4) conditions` TRUE `, (b3) building rights` FALSE `, the Director allowed` NOTHING `, (d)(4) excludes` FALSE `, company or liquidation` FALSE) `, the highest rate of section 121 being` (47%) `, the seller's other taxable income being` 0 `under the scale` `a flat scale at 47%` `, reading the forks as` `the default readings` EQUALS 3_385_189
-- (b4) does not oust (b1): section 48A(b4) disapplies (b2) and (b3) only, and (b1) opens "notwithstanding (b)(1)"; so a qualifying apartment bought before the change date with the (b4) conditions is taxed under (b1) (NOTES.md, assumption A14).
-- Bought 1 January 2010 (before the change date), the (b4) conditions hold: (b1) applies. Real betterment 13,340,756 = 3,652 x 3,653 ; the commencement day is before the purchase,
-- so part 1 is nought ; part 2 runs from the purchase day to 31 December 2011: 729 days between (730 both ends) over 3,652 (3,653).
--   Days between: part 2 = 3,653 x 729 = 2,663,037 ; part 3 = 13,340,756 - 2,663,037 = 10,677,719 ; tax 20% x 2,663,037 (532,607.4) + 25% x 10,677,719 (2,669,429.75) = 3,202,037.15 ;
--   plus 10% x 500,000 = 50,000 on the chargeable inflationary amount (a (b4) apartment is not a (b2) apartment): 3,252,037.15.
#ASSERT `retl 48A — the betterment tax on` (`the land sale by` (`an individual with the records` `no records`) `, land association action` FALSE `, betterment` 20_000_000 `, real betterment` 13_340_756 `, chargeable inflationary` 500_000 `, bought` (YMD 2010 1 1) `, sold` (YMD 2020 1 1) `, qualifying apartment` TRUE `, (b4) conditions` TRUE `, (b3) building rights` FALSE `, the Director allowed` NOTHING `, (d)(4) excludes` FALSE `, company or liquidation` FALSE) `, the highest rate of section 121 being` (47%) `, the seller's other taxable income being` 0 `under the scale` `a flat scale at 47%` `, reading the forks as` (`the default readings but the days counted as` `the days between the first day and the last day, the first not counted`) `and the collision of (b4) with (b1) as` `(b1) still applies, since it opens "notwithstanding (b)(1)"` EQUALS 3_252_037.15
-- (b3): additional building rights influenced the consideration: needs section 49Z; declined.
#ASSERT REFUSED `retl 48A — the betterment tax on` (`the land sale by` (`an individual with the records` `no records`) `, land association action` FALSE `, betterment` 20_000_000 `, real betterment` 13_340_756 `, chargeable inflationary` 500_000 `, bought` (YMD 2010 1 1) `, sold` (YMD 2020 1 1) `, qualifying apartment` TRUE `, (b4) conditions` FALSE `, (b3) building rights` TRUE `, the Director allowed` NOTHING `, (d)(4) excludes` FALSE `, company or liquidation` FALSE) `, the highest rate of section 121 being` (47%) `, the seller's other taxable income being` 0 `under the scale` `a flat scale at 47%` `, reading the forks as` `the default readings` BECAUSE "section 48A(b3) splits the sale value by the amounts of section 49Z, which this model does not encode"

§§ `Paragraph (d): old land (a body of persons at 23%; the betterment 1,000,000, the real betterment 900,000: the ordinary tax 900,000 x 23% = 207,000)`
-- Bought 1 June 1940, sold 30 June 2013; a company with business income: (d)(2): 12% (acquired up to tax year 1948) + 1% for each tax year from 2005.
--   A tax year begins on 1 April. 30 June 2013 is in the year that begins in 2013 (named 2013) or ends in 2014 (named 2014).
--   Named by the year it begins in: 2005 and 2013 both counted: 9 years: 21% ; not counting 2005: 8 years: 20%.
--   Named by the year it ends in:   2005 and 2014 both counted: 10 years: 22% ; not counting 2005: 9 years: 21%.
--   The tax is the lesser of 207,000 and the rate x 1,000,000 where the rate does not exceed 23%: 207,000 (21%: 210,000) ; 200,000 (20%) ; 207,000 (22%: 220,000) ; 207,000 (21%).
#ASSERT `retl 48A — the betterment tax on` (`the land sale by` (`a body of persons taxed at` (23%)) `, land association action` FALSE `, betterment` 1_000_000 `, real betterment` 900_000 `, chargeable inflationary` 0 `, bought` (YMD 1940 6 1) `, sold` (YMD 2013 6 30) `, qualifying apartment` FALSE `, (b4) conditions` FALSE `, (b3) building rights` FALSE `, the Director allowed` NOTHING `, (d)(4) excludes` FALSE `, company or liquidation` TRUE) `, the highest rate of section 121 being` (47%) `, the seller's other taxable income being` 0 `under the scale` `the scale of s 121(a)` `, reading the forks as` (`the default readings but the tax years named as` `named by the calendar year in which it begins` `and counted from 2005 as` `2005 is not counted: the years after it up to the tax year of the sale`) EQUALS 200_000
#ASSERT `retl 48A — the betterment tax on` (`the land sale by` (`a body of persons taxed at` (23%)) `, land association action` FALSE `, betterment` 1_000_000 `, real betterment` 900_000 `, chargeable inflationary` 0 `, bought` (YMD 1940 6 1) `, sold` (YMD 2013 6 30) `, qualifying apartment` FALSE `, (b4) conditions` FALSE `, (b3) building rights` FALSE `, the Director allowed` NOTHING `, (d)(4) excludes` FALSE `, company or liquidation` TRUE) `, the highest rate of section 121 being` (47%) `, the seller's other taxable income being` 0 `under the scale` `the scale of s 121(a)` `, reading the forks as` (`the default readings but the tax years named as` `named by the calendar year in which it begins` `and counted from 2005 as` `2005 and the tax year of the sale are both counted`) EQUALS 207_000
#ASSERT `retl 48A — the betterment tax on` (`the land sale by` (`a body of persons taxed at` (23%)) `, land association action` FALSE `, betterment` 1_000_000 `, real betterment` 900_000 `, chargeable inflationary` 0 `, bought` (YMD 1940 6 1) `, sold` (YMD 2013 6 30) `, qualifying apartment` FALSE `, (b4) conditions` FALSE `, (b3) building rights` FALSE `, the Director allowed` NOTHING `, (d)(4) excludes` FALSE `, company or liquidation` TRUE) `, the highest rate of section 121 being` (47%) `, the seller's other taxable income being` 0 `under the scale` `the scale of s 121(a)` `, reading the forks as` (`the default readings but the tax years named as` `named by the calendar year in which it ends` `and counted from 2005 as` `2005 is not counted: the years after it up to the tax year of the sale`) EQUALS 207_000
#ASSERT REFUSED `retl 48A — the betterment tax on` (`the land sale by` (`a body of persons taxed at` (23%)) `, land association action` FALSE `, betterment` 1_000_000 `, real betterment` 900_000 `, chargeable inflationary` 0 `, bought` (YMD 1940 6 1) `, sold` (YMD 2013 6 30) `, qualifying apartment` FALSE `, (b4) conditions` FALSE `, (b3) building rights` FALSE `, the Director allowed` NOTHING `, (d)(4) excludes` FALSE `, company or liquidation` TRUE) `, the highest rate of section 121 being` (47%) `, the seller's other taxable income being` 0 `under the scale` `the scale of s 121(a)` `, reading the forks as` `the default readings` BECAUSE "section 48A or section 88 leaves open a reading (the layer, the cap, the days of a period, who is a material shareholder, the naming of a tax year, or the years of paragraph (d)), and here the tax turns on it"
-- (d)(3) (not a company or a winding-up): sold 30 June 2013: named 2013: 2% + 2% x 1 = 4%: 16%: 160,000 ; named 2014: 2% + 2% x 2 = 6%: 18%: 180,000.
#ASSERT `retl 48A — the betterment tax on` (`the land sale by` (`a body of persons taxed at` (23%)) `, land association action` FALSE `, betterment` 1_000_000 `, real betterment` 900_000 `, chargeable inflationary` 0 `, bought` (YMD 1940 6 1) `, sold` (YMD 2013 6 30) `, qualifying apartment` FALSE `, (b4) conditions` FALSE `, (b3) building rights` FALSE `, the Director allowed` NOTHING `, (d)(4) excludes` FALSE `, company or liquidation` FALSE) `, the highest rate of section 121 being` (47%) `, the seller's other taxable income being` 0 `under the scale` `the scale of s 121(a)` `, reading the forks as` (`the default readings but the tax years named as` `named by the calendar year in which it begins` `and counted from 2005 as` `2005 and the tax year of the sale are both counted`) EQUALS 160_000
#ASSERT `retl 48A — the betterment tax on` (`the land sale by` (`a body of persons taxed at` (23%)) `, land association action` FALSE `, betterment` 1_000_000 `, real betterment` 900_000 `, chargeable inflationary` 0 `, bought` (YMD 1940 6 1) `, sold` (YMD 2013 6 30) `, qualifying apartment` FALSE `, (b4) conditions` FALSE `, (b3) building rights` FALSE `, the Director allowed` NOTHING `, (d)(4) excludes` FALSE `, company or liquidation` FALSE) `, the highest rate of section 121 being` (47%) `, the seller's other taxable income being` 0 `under the scale` `the scale of s 121(a)` `, reading the forks as` (`the default readings but the tax years named as` `named by the calendar year in which it ends` `and counted from 2005 as` `2005 and the tax year of the sale are both counted`) EQUALS 180_000
-- (d)(4) excludes (a right given without consideration, say): the ordinary tax 207,000.
#ASSERT `retl 48A — the betterment tax on` (`the land sale by` (`a body of persons taxed at` (23%)) `, land association action` FALSE `, betterment` 1_000_000 `, real betterment` 900_000 `, chargeable inflationary` 0 `, bought` (YMD 1940 6 1) `, sold` (YMD 2013 6 30) `, qualifying apartment` FALSE `, (b4) conditions` FALSE `, (b3) building rights` FALSE `, the Director allowed` NOTHING `, (d)(4) excludes` TRUE `, company or liquidation` FALSE) `, the highest rate of section 121 being` (47%) `, the seller's other taxable income being` 0 `under the scale` `the scale of s 121(a)` `, reading the forks as` `the default readings` EQUALS 207_000
-- Acquired 1 June 1961 (the tax year begins in 1961): (d) does not reach it: 207,000.
#ASSERT `retl 48A — the betterment tax on` (`the land sale by` (`a body of persons taxed at` (23%)) `, land association action` FALSE `, betterment` 1_000_000 `, real betterment` 900_000 `, chargeable inflationary` 0 `, bought` (YMD 1961 6 1) `, sold` (YMD 2013 6 30) `, qualifying apartment` FALSE `, (b4) conditions` FALSE `, (b3) building rights` FALSE `, the Director allowed` NOTHING `, (d)(4) excludes` FALSE `, company or liquidation` TRUE) `, the highest rate of section 121 being` (47%) `, the seller's other taxable income being` 0 `under the scale` `the scale of s 121(a)` `, reading the forks as` `the default readings` EQUALS 207_000
-- Sold 30 June 2017, (d)(3): named 2017: 12% + 2% + 2% x 5 = 24%, above the 23% of (a): the ordinary tax ; named 2018: 12% + 2% + 2% x 6 = 26%: the ordinary tax. 207,000 on every reading.
#ASSERT `retl 48A — the betterment tax on` (`the land sale by` (`a body of persons taxed at` (23%)) `, land association action` FALSE `, betterment` 1_000_000 `, real betterment` 900_000 `, chargeable inflationary` 0 `, bought` (YMD 1940 6 1) `, sold` (YMD 2017 6 30) `, qualifying apartment` FALSE `, (b4) conditions` FALSE `, (b3) building rights` FALSE `, the Director allowed` NOTHING `, (d)(4) excludes` FALSE `, company or liquidation` FALSE) `, the highest rate of section 121 being` (47%) `, the seller's other taxable income being` 0 `under the scale` `the scale of s 121(a)` `, reading the forks as` `the default readings` EQUALS 207_000

§§ `The date`
-- A sale on 31 December 2011 is before the change date: declined.
#ASSERT REFUSED `retl 48A — the betterment tax on` (`a plain land sale by` `someone with no records` `, real betterment` 200_000 `, chargeable inflationary` 0 `, bought` (YMD 2001 5 1) `, sold` (YMD 2011 12 31)) `, the highest rate of section 121 being` (47%) `, the seller's other taxable income being` 0 `under the scale` `the scale of s 121(a)` `, reading the forks as` `the default readings` BECAUSE "the deposited text of section 48A is the text as amended at retrieval, and the text for a sale before the change date, 1 January 2012, is not deposited"

§§ `Fork B4 (0.1.1): section 48A(b4) against section 48A(b1) for a qualifying apartment bought before the change date`
-- The 2010 apartment with the (b4) conditions (the arithmetic is above): (b1) still applies: 3,252,037.15 ; (b4) restores plain (b)(1): 13,340,756 x 25% = 3,335,189 and 10% x 500,000 = 50,000: 3,385,189.
-- The two differ, so the default declines. Bought 1 January 2013 the clauses do not collide ((b1) does not reach it) and every reading gives 3,385,189 (tested above).
#ASSERT `retl 48A — the betterment tax on` (`the land sale by` (`an individual with the records` `no records`) `, land association action` FALSE `, betterment` 20_000_000 `, real betterment` 13_340_756 `, chargeable inflationary` 500_000 `, bought` (YMD 2010 1 1) `, sold` (YMD 2020 1 1) `, qualifying apartment` TRUE `, (b4) conditions` TRUE `, (b3) building rights` FALSE `, the Director allowed` NOTHING `, (d)(4) excludes` FALSE `, company or liquidation` FALSE) `, the highest rate of section 121 being` (47%) `, the seller's other taxable income being` 0 `under the scale` `a flat scale at 47%` `, reading the forks as` (`the default readings but the days counted as` `the days between the first day and the last day, the first not counted`) `and the collision of (b4) with (b1) as` `(b4) restores plain (b)(1): the layered rates of (b1) do not apply` EQUALS 3_385_189
#ASSERT REFUSED `retl 48A — the betterment tax on` (`the land sale by` (`an individual with the records` `no records`) `, land association action` FALSE `, betterment` 20_000_000 `, real betterment` 13_340_756 `, chargeable inflationary` 500_000 `, bought` (YMD 2010 1 1) `, sold` (YMD 2020 1 1) `, qualifying apartment` TRUE `, (b4) conditions` TRUE `, (b3) building rights` FALSE `, the Director allowed` NOTHING `, (d)(4) excludes` FALSE `, company or liquidation` FALSE) `, the highest rate of section 121 being` (47%) `, the seller's other taxable income being` 0 `under the scale` `a flat scale at 47%` `, reading the forks as` (`the default readings but the days counted as` `the days between the first day and the last day, the first not counted`) BECAUSE "section 48A or section 88 leaves open a reading (the layer, the cap, the days of a period, who is a material shareholder, the naming of a tax year, or the years of paragraph (d)), and here the tax turns on it"

§§ `The parts partition the days (0.1.1): no day of the period is in two parts`
-- Real betterment equal to the number of days of the period (sold 1 January 2020), so that each part is its number of days. The days from the purchase day to 31 December 2011 are
-- change date - purchase day. With the Starting Day (7 November 2001) in the part after it, or in the part before it, part 1 + part 2 is that number.
--   bought 6 Nov 2001: D = 6,631 ; days to 31 Dec 2011 = 3,708.   bought 7 Nov 2001: D = 6,630 ; 3,707.   bought 8 Nov 2001: D = 6,629 ; 3,706.
GIVEN p  IS A DATE
      rb IS A NUMBER
      c  IS A `A reading of how the days of a period are counted`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the first two parts bought on` p `with the real betterment` rb `counting the days as` c MEANS
    `retl s 47 — the real betterment until the commencement day, of` rb `bought on` p `and sold on` (YMD 2020 1 1) `, counting the days as` c
    PLUS `retl s 47 — the real betterment after the commencement day up to the change date, of` rb `bought on` p `and sold on` (YMD 2020 1 1) `, counting the days as` c
#ASSERT `the first two parts bought on` (YMD 2001 11 6) `with the real betterment` 6631 `counting the days as` `both the first and the last day are counted` EQUALS 3_708
#ASSERT `the first two parts bought on` (YMD 2001 11 7) `with the real betterment` 6630 `counting the days as` `both the first and the last day are counted` EQUALS 3_707
#ASSERT `the first two parts bought on` (YMD 2001 11 8) `with the real betterment` 6629 `counting the days as` `both the first and the last day are counted` EQUALS 3_706
#ASSERT `the first two parts bought on` (YMD 2001 11 6) `with the real betterment` 6631 `counting the days as` `both ends counted, a boundary day belonging to the part before it` EQUALS 3_708
#ASSERT `the first two parts bought on` (YMD 2001 11 7) `with the real betterment` 6630 `counting the days as` `both ends counted, a boundary day belonging to the part before it` EQUALS 3_707
#ASSERT `the first two parts bought on` (YMD 2001 11 8) `with the real betterment` 6629 `counting the days as` `both ends counted, a boundary day belonging to the part before it` EQUALS 3_706
-- The days between: part 1 + part 2 is one day less than the interval, as the elapsed days between the purchase day and 31 December 2011 (D is one less, 6,630 for the first purchase day).
#ASSERT `the first two parts bought on` (YMD 2001 11 6) `with the real betterment` 6630 `counting the days as` `the days between the first day and the last day, the first not counted` EQUALS 3_707
-- A purchase on the Starting Day: part 1 is nought when the Starting Day is in the part after it, and one day when it is in the part before it.
#ASSERT `retl s 47 — the real betterment until the commencement day, of` 6630 `bought on` (YMD 2001 11 7) `and sold on` (YMD 2020 1 1) `, counting the days as` `both the first and the last day are counted` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `retl s 47 — the real betterment until the commencement day, of` 6630 `bought on` (YMD 2001 11 7) `and sold on` (YMD 2020 1 1) `, counting the days as` `both ends counted, a boundary day belonging to the part before it` EQUALS 1
